WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.312 --> 00:00:15.256
One afternoon Milly Snow visited Aunt Polly.

2
00:00:15.276 --> 00:00:21.658
"I came to find out how Pollyanna is doing," Milly said.

3
00:00:22.978 --> 00:00:25.239
Aunt Polly pushed back a loose strand of hair.

4
00:00:25.259 --> 00:00:29.460
"About the same, and how is your mother?"

5
00:00:30.952 --> 00:00:32.873
"That's what I want you to tell Pollyanna.

6
00:00:34.154 --> 00:00:38.296
Mother is so much better, and it's all thanks to Pollyanna and her game."

7
00:00:40.258 --> 00:00:43.740
Aunt Polly wanted to ask about the game, but Milly kept on talking.

8
00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:48.382
"Mother just used to sit in her dark room and complain.

9
00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:54.026
But now she keeps the curtains open and takes an interest in her appearance."

10
00:00:56.847 --> 00:00:57.548
"That's nice."

11
00:00:59.316 --> 00:01:04.941
"After Pollyanna told Mother she should be glad she has arms and hands, Mother wanted to do something

12
00:01:05.121 --> 00:01:13.027
useful. So she knits blankets for charity, and her room is full of brightly colored yarn.

13
00:01:15.429 --> 00:01:18.452
I used to hate to go in there, but now I'm glad to.

14
00:01:18.972 --> 00:01:21.674
Anyway Milly took a deep breath.

15
00:01:21.694 --> 00:01:28.660
"We thought if Pollyanna knew she'd changed our lives, she might be glad."

16
00:01:30.353 --> 00:01:31.414
Milly stood up to go.

17
00:01:31.434 --> 00:01:33.836
"So will you tell her?"

18
00:01:33.856 --> 00:01:40.361
"Of course," Aunt Polly said, though she wasn't quite sure what Milly had been talking about.

19
00:01:42.803 --> 00:01:45.845
Many other visitors left mysterious messages for Pollyanna.

20
00:01:48.287 --> 00:01:51.590
When Widow Benton arrived, she was dressed in black as usual.

21
00:01:52.651 --> 00:01:55.113
But she was also wearing a blue ribbon around her neck.

22
00:01:56.414 --> 00:02:01.033
"Please tell Pollyanna about my ribbon," Widow Benton said to Aunt Polly.

23
00:02:01.053 --> 00:02:06.336
"I hope she'll be glad I've taken her suggestion to wear some color."

24
00:02:09.438 --> 00:02:11.719
That same day a stranger named Mrs.

25
00:02:11.799 --> 00:02:12.700
Tarbell arrived.

26
00:02:14.001 --> 00:02:16.522
She, too, was dressed in black, as if in mourning.

27
00:02:16.542 --> 00:02:22.726
"I've been staying at the hotel in town and taking long walks every day for my health.

28
00:02:24.147 --> 00:02:26.248
I always enjoyed walking with Pollyanna.

29
00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:31.063
She reminded me of my daughter who died years ago.

30
00:02:33.625 --> 00:02:35.787
Could you just tell her that I'm glad now?

31
00:02:36.227 --> 00:02:37.808
I'd rather not explain why."

32
00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:40.470
After Mrs.

33
00:02:40.531 --> 00:02:43.053
Tarbell left, Aunt Polly hurried upstairs.

34
00:02:43.073 --> 00:02:47.056
"Pollyanna, do you know a Mrs.

35
00:02:47.196 --> 00:02:50.419
Tarbell?" "Oh, yes.

36
00:02:51.019 --> 00:02:53.061
She's awfully sick and sad.

37
00:02:54.262 --> 00:02:56.224
We go for long walks together.

38
00:02:57.628 --> 00:03:04.671
I mean, we used to Pollyanna's voice broke, and two big tears rolled down her cheeks.

39
00:03:07.032 --> 00:03:08.313
Aunt Polly cleared her throat.

40
00:03:09.813 --> 00:03:11.974
"She said to tell you she's glad now."

41
00:03:13.995 --> 00:03:16.456
Pollyanna clapped her hands and almost smiled.

42
00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:19.637
"Oh, I'm so glad!"

43
00:03:19.657 --> 00:03:22.979
"She said something about a game.

44
00:03:24.119 --> 00:03:25.400
What was she talking about?"

45
00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:30.062
"Nothing." Pollyanna turned her head away.

46
00:03:30.082 --> 00:03:32.463
"I can't talk about it."

47
00:03:33.404 --> 00:03:36.506
Pollyanna seemed so upset that Aunt Polly left her alone.

48
00:03:39.027 --> 00:03:41.689
She went downstairs to the kitchen, where Nancy was ironing.

49
00:03:41.709 --> 00:03:48.633
"Nancy! All of Pollyanna's visitors want me to tell her they're playing some game.

50
00:03:49.673 --> 00:03:54.376
Half the town is wearing bright colors or doing new things all because of Pollyanna.

51
00:03:55.324 --> 00:03:57.586
I tried to ask her about it, but she wouldn't tell me."

52
00:03:58.907 --> 00:04:00.348
Aunt Polly stamped her foot.

53
00:04:00.368 --> 00:04:04.772
"What is this absurd game everyone's playing?"

54
00:04:06.233 --> 00:04:09.736
To Aunt Polly's surprise and dismay, Nancy burst into tears.

55
00:04:12.038 --> 00:04:16.642
When Nancy had calmed down, she told the story of the doll and the crutches in the donation

56
00:04:16.682 --> 00:04:20.625
box. "She was glad for crutches?"

57
00:04:21.746 --> 00:04:23.328
Aunt Polly choked back a sob.

58
00:04:26.656 --> 00:04:29.638
"But why wouldn't she tell me about the Glad Game?"

59
00:04:31.399 --> 00:04:34.961
Nancy picked up the napkin she'd just ironed and wrung it like a wet rag.

60
00:04:34.981 --> 00:04:39.484
"Begging your pardon, ma'am, but you wouldn't let her.

61
00:04:40.524 --> 00:04:44.347
You told her not to speak of her father, and it was his game.

62
00:04:46.588 --> 00:04:52.631
Pollyanna desperately wanted to play it, so she told a few people, and the game spread throughout the

63
00:04:52.751 --> 00:05:00.312
town. She was always so cheerful Nancy tried to smooth the wrinkled napkin.

64
00:05:00.332 --> 00:05:04.135
"Now everyone is sad she isn't glad anymore."

65
00:05:04.155 --> 00:05:09.880
"Well, I know someone who'll play that game with her right now!"

66
00:05:11.541 --> 00:05:14.163
Aunt Polly hurried back upstairs to Pollyanna's room.

67
00:05:15.164 --> 00:05:20.408
When she told Pollyanna that Nancy had explained the game to her, Pollyanna's face lit up with joy.

68
00:05:21.892 --> 00:05:26.396
"Oh, Aunt Polly, you're the person I've most wanted to play the Glad Game with!"

69
00:05:27.557 --> 00:05:30.740
Pollyanna held out her arms, and Aunt Polly hugged her.

70
00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:35.965
"Do you have any idea what you've accomplished?"

71
00:05:37.106 --> 00:05:38.727
Aunt Polly smiled broadly.

72
00:05:38.747 --> 00:05:44.833
"The whole town is happier because you taught everyone the Glad Game."

73
00:05:46.554 --> 00:05:48.356
Pollyanna suddenly looked serious.

74
00:05:49.724 --> 00:05:52.509
"I'm so glad I had legs that worked.

75
00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:55.974
Because without them, I couldn't have done that!"
